{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Azeret it is.</b> A parable: to a king whose sons came to greet him. The first time, he said to them: when will you return to me? They said to him: in fifty days. He sent them off in peace. The second time, he said to them: when will you return? They said to him: in four months. He sent them off in peace. The third time, they said to him: we cannot return until after seven months. He said to them: if so, I ask of you, stay with me one more day, so that I may be sated with the sight of you, since you are delaying so long. Therefore there is no azeret for Israel at Pesach, because they return at Shavuot; and not at Shavuot, because they return at Sukkot. But at Sukkot, since they do not return until Pesach because of the rains, the Holy One, blessed be He, holds them back one day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:44.328364655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}